### rk3566-opp-2ghz

Adds a 1992 MHz CPU OPP at 1.2 V for RK3566 overclocking.
If the board limits vdd_cpu below 1.2 V, the OPP falls back to about 1.15 V, and the real speed gain depends on the chip and may be none.
If the limit is below 1.15 V, the kernel disables the OPP.
On RK3568, the overlay raises the stock 1992 MHz OPP to 1.2 V if the board allows it.
Images built before this overlay limit the CPU to 1800 MHz at boot. To remove the limit, set MAX_SPEED=1992000 in /etc/default/cpufrequtils.
Under sustained full load, the CPU can reach the 70 °C throttle point.
WARNING! Not officially supported by Rockchip!!!
